step 4 -- a verdict for each month that differs
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2024-03   platform is 486,250.00 BELOW finance  (-1.15%)
   what was checked:
     - all 372 store-days present, no gap in any bill sequence
     - both reconstructions of March agree to 0.00
     - the shortfall is exactly 486,250.00, round to the rupee,
       in a month whose other figures carry real paise
     - no bill and no store-day in March is worth that amount:
        bills_of_that_value  store_days_of_that_value
                          0                         0
   verdict: DEFINITION / SCOPE.  The amount is not in the till data in any
     form, and the till data for March is internally complete and
     self-consistent.  Something finance counted in March never passed
     through a till -- a manual adjustment, an accrual, or a channel that
     does not bill through the POS.  A perfectly round figure is what a
     journal entry looks like, not what 60,000 shopping baskets look like.

2024-07   platform is 232,131.70 BELOW finance  (-0.57%)
   what was checked:
     - three store-days never arrived: S07 (Pune), 9/10/11 July, Tue-Thu
       -- exactly the outage billing_notes.md records
     - valuing those three days on S07's own Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday
       averages for July gives 222,193.07 against a gap of 232,131.70
     - residual -9,938.63 (-4.3%), which is within the
       day-to-day spread of a single store
   verdict: SOURCE DATA.  The exports do not exist and never will.  Finance
     has the numbers because the store phoned them in.

2024-12   platform is 50.48 ABOVE finance  (+0.00010%)
   what was checked:
     - all 372 store-days present, no gap in any bill sequence
     - both reconstructions of December agree to 0.00
     - the paise on each finance figure:
         month  revenue_inr  paise
       2024-01  38446071.33     33
       2024-02  34887085.55     55
       2024-03  42457899.09      9
       2024-04  37958457.37     37
       2024-05  41764716.40     40
       2024-06  38987082.82     82
       2024-07  40527291.81     81
       2024-08  45252181.75     75
       2024-09  44615037.46     46
       2024-10  56359195.92     92
       2024-11  51583838.47     47
       2024-12  50745209.00      0
     - December is the ONLY month finance closed on a whole rupee
   verdict: not worth calling a cause.  0.0001% -- one part in a million --
     on the one month whose signed-off figure ends in .00 while the other
     eleven carry real paise.  That is a hand-keyed or rounded close, not a
     data problem and not a pipeline problem.  The platform's figure is the
     supportable one; it should be noted, not escalated.
==============================================================================
step 5 -- which of the three goes back to the finance team
==============================================================================

Of the three causes, the one to take to finance is the DEFINITION difference:
March 2024.

  Why that one.  It is the only difference that is about what revenue MEANS,
  and it is the only one that will recur silently.  486,250.00 is 1.15% of the
  month.  If finance books adjustments outside the POS, the platform can never
  derive them and the dashboard will sit permanently below the closed books --
  and nobody will know which of the two numbers is wrong.  The ask is narrow:
  what is the 486,250.00 in March, and is it a standing practice?  Then it
  becomes a documented adjustment line in the model, and the two agree by
  construction instead of by luck.

  Why not the other two.

  July is a SOURCE problem and it is not finance's to solve.  It belongs to
  the billing vendor and the ops desk: three exports were never produced.
  What is needed FROM finance is only the phoned-in figures for those three
  days, so the gap can be booked as a named adjustment rather than left as an
  unexplained 232,131.70.  The fix is a process one -- an arrival check that
  notices a missing store-day the next morning instead of eight months later.

  December is not a cause at all.  Fifty rupees on fifty million, on the one
  month closed to a whole rupee.  Raising it would spend the credibility that
  the other two need.

  And the fourth possibility, a bug in this pipeline, is the one that was
  ruled out first rather than last: the two independent reconstructions agree
  to 0.00 in all twelve months, every one of 165,704 bills balances against
  its own lines, and nine months land on finance's signed-off figure exactly.

